Real oscillators lose energy. For a viscous drag force the equation of motion becomes

$ m dot.double(x) + b dot(x) + k x = 0 quad arrow.r.double quad dot.double(x) + 2 gamma dot(x) + omega_0^2 x = 0, $

with damping rate $gamma = b slash 2m$. The trial solution $e^(lambda t)$ gives $lambda = -gamma plus.minus sqrt(gamma^2 - omega_0^2)$, and three regimes follow.
